From 0a7d75b7aa78d1ac24aa22a9f93eaa208ba4a7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: G-Su Paek <gsu.paek@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:39:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Security hardening: CSP, dead server code, calendar commits,
 Hot Pot feed

- Move each page's CSP <meta> to the top of <head> and remove all inline
  scripts (GA bootstrap -> analytics.js, coaching calculator -> coaching.js);
  drop 'unsafe-inline' from coaching.html; add form-action everywhere.
- Hot Pot videos load from same-origin hotpot.json built by update-videos.js
  in the Action; remove the api.allorigins.win proxy from code and CSP.
- update-calendar.js no longer rewrites calendar.json when nothing changed
  (was producing a commit every 15 min) and detects venue/link edits.
- Remove unused Express/SQLite/nodemailer server and its dependencies.
- Rewrite _headers with a note that GitHub Pages ignores it; stop marking
  unfingerprinted JS/CSS as immutable.
- Centralize the visitor counter in utils.js (one place to switch projects).
- Add Supabase SQL to lock down comments.token and pin function search_path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbmG3YATjwJfPCp13EhaK8
